fix(cs): propagate CS_SIGNED for a validated signature

launchd aborts its first boot task on this port:

  initproc exited -- exit reason namespace 7 subcode 0x1
  failed to get the code signing identity for a boot-task
  (mount-phase-1, /sbin/mount) errno: 2

cs_identity_get() returns NULL unless proc_getcsflags() carries CS_SIGNED, and
csproc_get_blob() refuses to hand out a blob for the same reason.  CS_SIGNED is
an AMFI bit on Apple platforms, so it is deliberately absent from the
load_result.csflags mask in exec_mach_imgact(), and the port never set it: every
identity and entitlement path therefore behaved as though the process were
unsigned.  Propagate it from the same CS_VALID decision that already gates the
blob, so the flag cannot claim more than the blob proves.  kebab_cs still decides
what is trusted; this only makes the process's flags agree with the blob that was
attached.
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -1432,6 +1432,22 @@
 		imgp->ip_csflags |= CS_PLATFORM_BINARY;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * CS_SIGNED is AMFI's bit as well, which is why it is absent from the mask
+	 * above: on Apple platforms AMFI sets it when a trust cache vouches for the
+	 * blob.  This port replaces AMFI with kebab_cs, and a blob that validated
+	 * already carries CS_VALID from cs_blob_init_validated().  Without
+	 * CS_SIGNED every csproc_get_blob() caller behaves as though the process
+	 * were unsigned, so cs_identity_get() returns NULL and launchd aborts a
+	 * boot task with "failed to get the code signing identity" (namespace 7,
+	 * subcode 0x1).  Propagating it from the same CS_VALID decision cannot
+	 * claim more than the blob proves, and it does not widen kebab_cs's
+	 * policy: a blob that did not validate never reaches this point.
+	 */
+	if (load_result.csflags & CS_VALID) {
+		imgp->ip_csflags |= CS_SIGNED; /* kebab: propagate validated signature */
+	}
+
 	if (proc_getcsflags(p) & CS_EXEC_SET_HARD) {
 		imgp->ip_csflags |= CS_HARD;
 	}
